    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d950">

                <pb facs="0734" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg618"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13729.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-09T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 9, 1914, 11 a.m. No.
                        2</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Carranza has issued another manifesto disowning the Convention and its
                    proceedings, calling on all proxies to retire from the Convention at or before 6
                    p.m. of the 10th to report to principals, and on all generals personally in
                    attendance to retire at the same time and take immediate charge of their
                    commands; otherwise, the officer next in grade to assume command and hold
                    election to select successor to the disobedient general. All government
                    officials and employees are reminded that the acts of the Convention are
                    disowned and that no orders are to be obeyed except those from the First
                    Chief.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
